  "interpretation": [
    "Managed allocated bytes decreased by 8.4986% and copied bytes by 4.8858% in this single diagnostic comparison; major-GC-sampled maximum live bytes increased by 6.8343%, RTS memory by 4.9505%, and process maximum RSS by 4.8659%.",
    "The major-GC residency observations were sampled 84 times for A-stats and 79 times for C-stats, at different collection schedules. They are not a continuous matched peak-live trace.",
    "Managed allocation volume, copied bytes, sampled live maximum, RTS memory/fragmentation and process RSS are distinct quantities. The results do not identify the cause of the historical RSS cost or attribute an exact byte saving to a particular closure or source call.",
    "The reported fragmentation is 0 MiB on both sides, a limited aggregate with whole-MiB truncation. It does not establish zero allocator slack, pinned-object fragmentation or OS-level fragmentation. Maximum slop is a separate counter. RTS memory and process RSS maxima need not occur simultaneously; their difference is not a partition of memory.",
    "One fixed A-stats then C-stats diagnostic, zero performance samples. New relinked layouts and baked statistics differ from historical producers. No speedup estimate, stability/significance claim, merge readiness, or pooling with the earlier Frontend CAAC, Async or Foundation windows.",
    "Original Frontend raw and ordered-query gates passed after each diagnostic. No extra qualification calls, retries, adaptive additions or native/fixed-point calls."
